WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.246
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online TOEFL preparation.

2
00:00:05.546 --> 00:00:08.770
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.070 --> 00:00:17.701
Unit eighteen: Speaking: Fluency, Pronunciation and Development. Today you will improve how smoothly, clearly and fully you speak.

4
00:00:18.001 --> 00:00:20.758
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:21.700 --> 00:00:24.712
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:25.550 --> 00:00:26.563
Fluency.

7
00:00:27.550 --> 00:00:30.850
Fluency means speaking smoothly without long pauses.

8
00:00:31.450 --> 00:00:33.496
Fluency improves with practice.

9
00:00:34.083 --> 00:00:36.689
Your turn. Say: Fluency.

10
00:00:39.533 --> 00:00:40.511
Fluency.

11
00:00:41.250 --> 00:00:42.321
Pronunciation.

12
00:00:43.317 --> 00:00:46.303
Pronunciation means the way you say sounds and words.

13
00:00:46.917 --> 00:00:48.707
Practise your pronunciation.

14
00:00:49.317 --> 00:00:52.120
Your turn. Say: Pronunciation.

15
00:00:54.967 --> 00:00:56.421
Pronunciation.

16
00:00:57.183 --> 00:00:58.068
Pace.

17
00:00:59.083 --> 00:01:01.153
Pace means the speed of your speech.

18
00:01:01.750 --> 00:01:03.355
Use a steady pace.

19
00:01:03.950 --> 00:01:06.521
Your turn. Say: Pace.

20
00:01:09.367 --> 00:01:10.194
Pace.

21
00:01:10.950 --> 00:01:11.847
Linking.

22
00:01:12.850 --> 00:01:16.034
Linking means joining words smoothly in speech.

23
00:01:16.650 --> 00:01:18.441
Linking makes speech natural.

24
00:01:19.050 --> 00:01:21.331
Your turn. Say: Linking.

25
00:01:24.167 --> 00:01:25.040
Linking.

26
00:01:25.783 --> 00:01:26.494
Vowel.

27
00:01:27.483 --> 00:01:30.029
Vowel means a sound like a, e, i, o, u.

28
00:01:30.617 --> 00:01:32.140
Practise the long vowel.

29
00:01:32.750 --> 00:01:35.228
Your turn. Say: Vowel.

30
00:01:38.067 --> 00:01:38.917
Vowel.

31
00:01:39.683 --> 00:01:40.731
Self-correct.

32
00:01:41.717 --> 00:01:44.308
Self-correct means to fix your own mistake.

33
00:01:44.917 --> 00:01:46.498
Self-correct quickly.

34
00:01:47.083 --> 00:01:49.596
Your turn. Say: Self-correct.

35
00:01:52.433 --> 00:01:53.434
Self-correct.

36
00:01:54.183 --> 00:01:55.022
Filler.

37
00:01:56.017 --> 00:01:58.841
Filler means a word like um that fills a pause.

38
00:01:59.450 --> 00:02:01.403
Avoid too many fillers.

39
00:02:02.017 --> 00:02:04.356
Your turn. Say: Filler.

40
00:02:07.200 --> 00:02:08.131
Filler.

41
00:02:08.883 --> 00:02:09.710
Record.

42
00:02:10.717 --> 00:02:13.413
Record means to save your voice to listen later.

43
00:02:14.017 --> 00:02:15.889
Record yourself every day.

44
00:02:16.483 --> 00:02:19.020
Your turn. Say: Record.

45
00:02:21.867 --> 00:02:22.903
Record.

46
00:02:23.700 --> 00:02:27.780
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:28.617 --> 00:02:31.011
Visal, what makes speaking sound fluent?

48
00:02:32.117 --> 00:02:40.284
A steady pace, few long pauses and natural linking between words. You do not need to be fast, but you need to keep moving.

49
00:02:41.383 --> 00:02:43.232
How do I improve pronunciation?

50
00:02:44.317 --> 00:02:54.005
Focus on stress and clear vowel sounds, not on an accent. Record yourself, listen back and compare with a model speaker.

51
00:02:55.117 --> 00:02:57.093
How do I develop my ideas?

52
00:02:58.183 --> 00:03:08.916
Use phrases like for instance, because of that and as a result. Fillers such as well are fine in small amounts, but too many make answers weak.

53
00:03:10.067 --> 00:03:11.683
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:12.517 --> 00:03:17.697
Grammar focus: Strategy: steady pace, clear sounds, full ideas.

55
00:03:17.997 --> 00:03:19.207
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:19.917 --> 00:03:22.799
I record myself and listen for long pauses.

57
00:03:23.683 --> 00:03:26.821
As a result, my answers sound smoother and more complete.

58
00:03:27.767 --> 00:03:35.516
Practise at a steady pace, record yourself, and focus on stress and clear vowels. Develop each answer with a reason and a result.

59
00:03:36.250 --> 00:03:40.388
Be careful! Don't say: I speak very fast to sound fluent.

60
00:03:42.333 --> 00:03:44.704
Say: I use a steady pace.

61
00:03:45.004 --> 00:03:46.342
Speak steadily.

62
00:03:47.133 --> 00:03:50.169
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

63
00:03:50.967 --> 00:03:52.409
Practice Every Day.

64
00:03:52.709 --> 00:03:55.788
Sovann records one answer every evening.

65
00:03:56.800 --> 00:03:59.543
He listens for pauses and unclear words.

66
00:04:00.533 --> 00:04:02.812
He repeats the answer with a steadier pace.

67
00:04:03.800 --> 00:04:07.367
He adds for instance and as a result to develop his ideas.

68
00:04:08.367 --> 00:04:10.889
After a month his speaking sounds smoother.

69
00:04:12.000 --> 00:04:15.979
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

70
00:04:16.817 --> 00:04:18.178
Fluency means blank.

71
00:04:18.478 --> 00:04:23.826
A, smooth speaking. B, very fast speaking. C, silent reading.

72
00:04:27.367 --> 00:04:29.900
The answer is A: smooth speaking.

73
00:04:31.050 --> 00:04:33.038
To record yourself helps you blank.

74
00:04:33.338 --> 00:04:38.094
A, sleep. B, listen and improve. C, avoid practice.

75
00:04:41.633 --> 00:04:44.109
The answer is B: listen and improve.

76
00:04:45.250 --> 00:04:47.342
Too many fillers make answers blank.

77
00:04:47.642 --> 00:04:50.982
A, stronger. B, longer. C, weaker.

78
00:04:54.533 --> 00:04:56.556
The answer is C: weaker.

79
00:04:57.717 --> 00:05:00.285
What does Sovann add to develop ideas?

80
00:05:00.585 --> 00:05:04.552
A, for instance. B, goodbye. C, a question.

81
00:05:08.100 --> 00:05:10.494
The answer is A: for instance.

82
00:05:11.650 --> 00:05:14.462
Pronunciation practice should focus on blank.

83
00:05:14.762 --> 00:05:20.029
A, speed only. B, stress and vowels. C, a perfect accent only.

84
00:05:23.567 --> 00:05:25.938
The answer is B: stress and vowels.

85
00:05:27.133 --> 00:05:30.598
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

86
00:05:31.450 --> 00:05:33.763
How do you improve your speaking fluency?

87
00:05:42.550 --> 00:05:44.201
Now listen to Visal.

88
00:05:44.501 --> 00:05:59.637
I practise at a steady pace and record myself to find long pauses and unclear sounds. I focus on stress and clear vowels, not on a perfect accent. I also develop my answers with a reason and an example.

89
00:05:59.937 --> 00:06:01.635
Excellent answer, Visal!

90
00:06:02.550 --> 00:06:09.150
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and strategy: steady pace, clear sounds, full ideas.

91
00:06:09.450 --> 00:06:13.855
Today's value is perseverance. Keep trying, even when it is hard.

92
00:06:14.155 --> 00:06:16.691
See you in Unit nineteen. Goodbye!

93
00:06:16.991 --> 00:06:19.632
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

